              "input_validation": "Field validation is reported separately; it does not change what this log line contains.",
              "use_protection": "Logging evidence: request  field email has a personal-data field-name hint and its content is written to the log; request  field password has a credential field-name hint and its content is written to the log. Assessed logging exposure: vulnerable (data class credential, content yes, redaction no). Verified logger binding and source evidence, with consistent answers that sensitive content reaches the log without redaction; this is a static judgment, not runtime confirmation.",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Keep credential and personal-data content out of logs",
                "actions": [
                  "Change the observed operation at app/api/auth/login/route.ts:16: logger.warn(\n      {\n        email,\n        password,\n        flag: LOGIN_FLAG,\n        route: \"/api/auth/login\",\n        action: \"login_attempt\",\n      },\n      `[auth] login attempt email=${email} password=${password} flag=${LOGIN_FLAG}`\n    )",
                  "Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.",
                  "Remove the value from the log entry, or log a non-revealing fact (presence, length, match result, or a non-reversible identifier) instead.",
                  "Log an allowlist of fields rather than whole request bodies, queries, or header sets. Never log Authorization or Cookie header values.",
                  "If redaction is required, apply a verified redaction before the logger call or in the logger's configuration, and test that emitted lines no longer contain the value.",
                  "Do not send credentials in URL query strings; access logs, proxies, and browser history record URLs. Use a request body or header instead."
                ],
