              "use_protection": "Path assessment: traversal vulnerable, containment none, coverage incomplete. Scanner policy: A consistent traversal answer is supported by an independent source-to-operand path with a verified fs/promises.readFile binding under the declared posix assumption; no enforced containment is established. Unresolved sibling paths remain visible. This is a static judgment, not runtime exploitation, symbolic-link or filesystem-state analysis, or independent Findings Review.",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed. The platform assumption is posix; Windows path semantics are not modeled. Unresolved sibling paths, if any, remain separate blocking or coverage records.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Contain this file operation",
                "actions": [
                  "At app/api/files/route.ts:62, constrain the path built from searchParams before readFile(filePath, \"utf-8\"). Do not rely on path.join, path.resolve, os.path.join or normalization alone, a '..' text check, a try/except around the call, or an error response after the read.",
                  "Prefer selecting the file by a trusted identifier (a finite allow-list of known names or a stored record id) instead of accepting a path.",
                  "Otherwise resolve the final path and verify it stays inside the trusted directory at a path-component boundary (a separator-bounded prefix, a path.relative or os.path.commonpath check) before the file operation, rejecting on failure. A join, resolve or normalize call, a '..' blacklist and a prefix comparison without a separator are not containment.",
